+## `BbPluginApi.experimental_p6rRoutes`
+
+**What it does.** Returns BB-owned canonical browser paths to backend plugins.
+It currently exposes thread paths and centralizes the personal project's
+projectless `/threads/:threadId` route rather than making plugins infer routing
+from a project id. It deliberately preserves client-core's existing raw-ID
+route behavior; validation and encoding stay at the route caller's boundary.
+
+**Audit before stabilizing.** Confirm every browser client still accepts each
+derived path, decide whether URL origin construction belongs in this API or at
+the caller's transport boundary, and add route kinds only when they have the
+same cross-client ownership and compatibility guarantees.
+
 ## `BbPluginApi.experimental_facets`
 
 **What it does.** Lets a plugin declare an enum-valued, shared-thread
